The TypeScript adaptation is a stateless per-frame transform of the chain's
negotiated format. It refuses, instead of approximating, the curves that need
libm (qsin, esin, hsin, log, cbr, exp, iqsin, ihsin, dese, losi, sinc, isinc,
quatr, qsin2, hsin2), runtime commands, timeline enable, expressions, numeric
curve and type values, values above 2^53, non-finite floating input, and the
configurations whose native output depends on native frame boundaries that
the chain does not reproduce. acrossfade is not adapted. The original source
and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
